# Ben's Burritos, the pack in words (content-burrito, 2026-11-09)

`packs/burrito/pack.js` (pack version 1), the second restaurant to unlock (left arm, lower). Format:
`docs/api/pack-format.md`; the line `docs/api/line.md`; the script `docs/api/script.md`; sounds `docs/api/audio.md`;
the food `docs/api/world.md` and `docs/api/food.md`. Worked example: the Pizza Parlor (`docs/api/packs/pizza.md`).
**food-burrito works from section 10** (every look, set, flourish and cook to draw). **The script works from
section 12** (every moment and who must say it).

**Check it** (from the game folder):

```
node -e "const B=require('./tests/bot.cjs'),SC=require('./js/core/script.js'),R=B.restaurants().find(r=>r.id==='burrito');console.log(B.schema.validate(R.pack),SC.check(R.pack,R.script),SC.coverage(R.pack,R.script))"
node -e "console.table(require('./tests/bot.cjs').pressReport('burrito'))"
BB_PACKS=burrito node --test "tests/*.test.cjs"
```

## 1. At a glance

| | |
|---|---|
| id, name | `burrito`, "Ben's Burritos" (court: "Burritos", left arm, slot 2, locked at the start, the 2nd to unlock) |
| version | 1 |
| format | `3`: `packs/burrito/script.js` covers every moment (content-burrito, 2026-11-09; the script in words: `docs/api/packs/burrito-script.md`) |
| manager | `{ id: 'mitch', art: 'mitch-burrito' }`: red bandana, green apron, a hot-sauce-stained badge (tie and taped badge underneath) |
| backdrops | `counter`, and by station `prep` (prep, chips) and `griddle` (griddle). All three exist (`BBArt.burrito`) |
| courses | `['main', 'side']`: burritos, bowls and tacos are mains; chips and salsa the side |
| levels | `{}`: the engine's ladder unchanged |
| no paging | protein and hot sauce have 4 values (4 answers, Ticket, Pause), every other pick 3; nothing pages, nothing repeats |

## 2. The line: stations and steps

| Station | backdrop | Steps, in order | redo | tool | sounds |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `prep` "Burrito Line" | `prep` | Pick `style` → Pick `rice` and Pick `beans` (burritos and bowls) → Pick `protein` → Add, one each: cheese, lettuce, pico, corn, sour cream, guacamole, jalapeños, onions (tacos only) → Pick `sauce` → the flourishes by themselves: `wrap` (burritos, show `burritoWrap`), `fold` (tacos, `tacoFold`), `arrange` (bowls, `bowlArrange`), then `burst` (the Everything Burrito and the Challenge Burrito, `burritoBurst`) | "Redo the Fillings" | | `{ auto: 'wrap' }` (add: `plop`) |
| `griddle` "Griddle" | `griddle` | Cook, stage set `toast`, `want: 'toast'` (the item: a wrapped burrito, or the tacos) | "Toast Again" | `grillPress` | `{ cook: 'press' }` |
| `chips` "Chip Basket" | `prep` | Pick `salsa` → Add guacamole → Add lime | "Redo the Chips" | | (add: `plop`) |

A burrito runs prep → griddle; tacos prep → griddle; a bowl prep only (it is never toasted); chips and salsa the chip
basket. The `when` steps read the ticket (never what was picked), so the same ticket always asks the same steps:
tacos never ask rice or beans and always ask onions; nothing else changes by order.

What the player hears (words.js; Timed changes only the griddle):

- "Burrito Line. Style: Burrito, Bowl or Tacos?" → "Rice: White, Brown or None?" → "Beans: Black, Pinto or None?" →
  "Protein: Chicken, Steak, Veggies or None?" → "Cheese." Add / Skip, then "Lettuce.", "Pico.", "Corn.", "Sour
  cream.", "Guacamole.", "Jalapeños." (tacos: "Onions.") → "Hot Sauce: Mild, Medium, Hot or None?" → the wrap (or the
  fold, or the bowl settling) plays by itself. A bad one: "The brown guacamole." Add / Skip / Swap It; on a pick, "Black
  beans with a hair in them" sits among the answers with Swap It.
- "Griddle. How toasted?" Lightly Toasted / Toasted / Extra Crispy. Timed: "Griddle. Lift the press when it is right.",
  one button **Lift the Press** (said "Lift the press. Toasted"); left on, it stops at Burnt.
- "Chips and Salsa. Salsa: Red, Green or Mango?" (a fresh item on a two-item order is named by the item) → "Guacamole."
  Add / Skip → "Lime." Add / Skip. A bad salsa: "Red salsa with a fly in it" among the answers, with Swap It.
- Review: "Here it is." Ring It Up, Redo the Fillings, Toast Again (with chips, Redo… as a row when there are more than
  three).

**Toppings are Add steps, not a repeat pick** (pilot.md 5.2): the brown guacamole sits on one, Sal's lettuce and
Oakes's onions are held as recipe parts, and nothing hides behind More….

**Changes to the brief, and why:**

- **Onions, tacos only.** Spec 5.4 and 2.3 have Oakes hate onions "in every pack that has them (pico does not count)",
  and the brief's toppings have none. Street tacos come with onions, so tacos ask one more Add (onions) and skip rice
  and beans; burritos stay at the level-1 budget of 14.
- **"Veggies"**, not "Veggie": the protein value reads the same on the answer ("Veggies") and on the ticket ("veggies").
- **The style is fixed by the recipe** (its name says it: Chicken Burrito, Chicken Bowl, Steak Tacos), so the first
  answer always matches the name on the ticket. The ticket says "burrito style", "bowl style", "taco style".
- **The toast is a `want`** (the recipe slot `toast`), so the customer says it in line order ("Steak Burrito, white
  rice, black beans, mild sauce, toasted"); a `done` would be said first ("Steak Burrito, toasted, white rice…").
- **The burst is a flourish, not a gross-out** (spec 4.6): the Everything Burrito always bursts after its wrap and is
  wrapped again in a second tortilla. That makes the odd order "a burrito wrapped inside another burrito" come true by
  accident. It is never random, never judged, never a mistake.
- **The fly is in the chips' salsa** (a pick of three), the hair in the beans (a pick of three), the brown on the
  guacamole (an Add on the line and at the chip basket).
- **A flourish for every style** (wrap, fold, arrange): a Motion Full shift always has one, and each style ends on its
  own small payoff.

## 3. Cooking: one stage set

| set | stages (first .. last) | Simple `choose` | ask | stop | speed |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `toast` | soft, lightlyToasted, toasted, extraCrispy, burnt | Lightly Toasted, Toasted, Extra Crispy | "How toasted?" | "Lift the Press" | pack `cookSpeeds` 12 / 8 / 5 s a stage, `wantedScale` 2 (the Burger Bar's grill) |

Stage names: Soft, Lightly Toasted, Toasted, Extra Crispy, Burnt. **Burnt is Timed's last stage** (one mistake,
`complain.done`), never a gross-out. Every griddled recipe names `toast: { pick: 'toast' }` in its slots (normal
Toasted); the Fire Burrito `{ pick: 'crispToast' }` (normal Extra Crispy).

## 4. Recipes

`level` is the only gate. Prices are the tip's base. "As written" is the ticket with the normal picks (change 0).

| id | Name | level | course | stations | price | As written (the ticket) | Can change |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `chickenBurrito` | Chicken Burrito | 1 | main | prep, griddle | 8 | burrito style, white rice, black beans, chicken, with cheese, lettuce, pico and sour cream, mild sauce, toasted | rice, beans, sauce, toast; holds lettuce, sour cream; adds corn, guacamole, jalapeños |
| `steakBurrito` | Steak Burrito | 1 | main | prep, griddle | 9 | burrito style, white rice, black beans, steak, with cheese, lettuce, pico, guacamole and jalapeños, mild sauce, toasted | picks; holds lettuce, guacamole; adds sour cream, corn |
| `beanCheese` | Bean and Cheese Burrito | 1 | main | prep, griddle | 6 | burrito style, rice: none, pinto beans, protein: none, with cheese, mild sauce, toasted | beans (`pintoBeans`), sauce, toast; adds pico, sour cream |
| `chickenBowl` | Chicken Bowl | 1 | main | prep | 8 | bowl style, white rice, black beans, chicken, with cheese, lettuce, pico, corn and sour cream, mild sauce | rice, beans, sauce; holds lettuce, sour cream; adds guacamole, jalapeños |
| `veggieBowl` | Veggie Bowl | 2 | main | prep | 8 | bowl style, white rice, black beans, veggies, with cheese, lettuce, pico, corn and guacamole, mild sauce | picks; holds cheese, lettuce; adds sour cream, jalapeños |
| `steakTacos` | Steak Tacos (plural "Plates of Steak Tacos") | 2 | main | prep, griddle | 9 | taco style, steak, with cheese, pico and onions, medium sauce, toasted | sauce (`tacoSauce`), toast; holds cheese, onions; adds lettuce, guacamole, jalapeños |
| `chickenTacos` | Chicken Tacos ("Plates of Chicken Tacos") | 2 | main | prep, griddle | 8 | taco style, chicken, with cheese, lettuce, pico, sour cream and onions, medium sauce, toasted | picks; holds lettuce, sour cream, onions; adds corn, guacamole |
| `chips` | Chips and Salsa ("Baskets of Chips and Salsa") | 2 | side | chips | 3 | red salsa, with lime | salsa; holds lime; adds guacamole |
| `everythingBurrito` | Everything Burrito | 3 | main | prep, griddle | 12 | burrito style, white rice, black beans, steak, with cheese, lettuce, pico, corn, sour cream, guacamole and jalapeños, mild sauce, toasted; **bursts and is wrapped again** | picks; holds lettuce, corn, jalapeños |
| `fireBurrito` | Fire Burrito | 3 | main | prep, griddle | 10 | burrito style, white rice, black beans, chicken, with cheese, pico, sour cream and jalapeños, hot sauce, extra crispy | rice, beans, toast (`crispToast`); holds sour cream; adds guacamole |
| `challengeBurrito` | Challenge Burrito | `'event'` | main | prep, griddle | 24 | burrito style, white rice, black beans, steak, with everything, hot sauce, toasted (the finale says extra crispy); `look: { shape: 'giantBurrito', giant: true }`; **bursts** | the finale only |

Slots and picks (level 5 uses the fancy lists):

| slot (question) | values (label; ticket words) | picks: values, normal, fancy |
|---|---|---|
| `style` "Style" | burrito "Burrito", bowl "Bowl", tacos "Tacos"; "burrito style", "bowl style", "taco style" | fixed by every recipe |
| `rice` "Rice" | whiteRice "White", brownRice "Brown", noRice "None"; "white rice", "rice: none" | `rice` white/brown, white, fancy + none |
| `beans` "Beans" | black "Black", pinto "Pinto", noBeans "None"; "black beans", "beans: none" | `beans` black/pinto, black, fancy + none; `pintoBeans` pinto/black, pinto |
| `protein` "Protein" | chicken "Chicken", steak "Steak", veggies "Veggies", noProtein "None"; "chicken", "protein: none" | fixed by every recipe |
| `sauce` "Hot Sauce" | mildSauce "Mild", mediumSauce "Medium", hotSauce "Hot", noSauce "None"; "mild sauce", "hot sauce: none" | `sauce` mild/medium/hot, mild, fancy + none; `tacoSauce` the same, normal medium |
| `salsa` "Salsa" | redSalsa "Red", greenSalsa "Green", mangoSalsa "Mango"; "red salsa" | `salsa` red/green, red, fancy + mango |
| (stage, `want`) | the `toast` set | `toast` lightly/toasted/extra crispy, toasted; `crispToast` extra crispy/toasted, extra crispy |

The value ids avoid every word js/core quotes (`medium`, `extra`, `done`, `one`, `two`, `plain`, `event`, `tutorial`):
`tests/pack.test.cjs` fails a pack id that js/core quotes, comments included.

**Combos** (level 3 up): one item, or two at the level's `more` odds: a main and chips and salsa, in that order. Never
two mains except Gus's two of one thing. Order Size "One Item" makes every order one item.

## 5. The ladder (`levels: {}`)

| Level | On offer | Items | Gross-outs | Extras |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | chicken, steak, bean and cheese burritos; chicken bowl | 1; at most 2 optional parts; change 0.2 | none | |
| 2 | + veggie bowl, steak tacos, chicken tacos, chips and salsa | 1; change 0.3 | none | |
| 3 | + Everything Burrito, Fire Burrito | 1 or 2: a main + chips | 0.3 an order, at most 2 a shift, never the first | |
| 4 | the same | as 3, change 0.4 | as 3 | one odd order at 50% a shift; one visitor (Reginald, Kai or Chef Hiro), never first |
| 5 | the same | as 4, change 0.5, fancy (None rice, beans and sauce; mango salsa) | 0.35, at most 2 | odd orders at 60%, `justTortilla` too |

Measured (300 five-order shifts a level in each mode, 1500 orders each, every one three stars with the right answers):
two-item orders 39% at level 3, 30% at 4, 35% at 5, 49% in the event (the finale is two); the hair in the beans about
60% of the gross-outs, the brown guacamole 25%, the fly in the salsa 15% (it needs chips on the order); level-4
visitors Reginald 37%, Chef Hiro 34%, Kai 28%; Sal never got lettuce, Oakes never onions, Inferno never a sauce but hot.

## 6. Ridiculous orders (level 4 and 5)

The customer says `order.odd.<id>` instead of the order; the ticket is plain and complete. At most one a shift, never
the first order or the visitor's. **An odd order is made as written** (normal picks: a `wants` does not reach it), so
Inferno, whose wants make everything hot, has only his own.

| id | level | recipe | the change | The ticket | Who | Presses |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `doubleWrap` | 4 | everythingBurrito | none: "a burrito wrapped inside another burrito" is said; the Everything Burrito bursts after its wrap and gets a second tortilla anyway | Everything Burrito as written | the regulars and Rita | 14 |
| `noAvocado` | 4 | veggieBowl | holds guacamole ("guacamole, but no avocado": guacamole is avocado) | Veggie Bowl: bowl style, white rice, black beans, veggies, with cheese, lettuce, pico and corn, mild sauce | the regulars and Rita | 13 |
| `hottest` | 4 | chickenBurrito | hot sauce ("the hottest you've got": they will cry, and say so) | Chicken Burrito: …, hot sauce, toasted | the regulars and Rita, never Inferno | 14 |
| `fireAlarm` | 4 | fireBurrito | extra crispy ("hot enough to set off the fire alarm", the one on the prep wall with the little mustache) | Fire Burrito as written | Inferno only | 14 |
| `justTortilla` | 5 | beanCheese | holds cheese; beans none, sauce none, lightly toasted ("just the tortilla") | Bean and Cheese Burrito: burrito style, rice: none, beans: none, protein: none, nothing else on it, hot sauce: none, lightly toasted (the name is the joke) | the regulars and Rita | 14 |

## 7. The five-star event: The Burrito Challenge

```js
events: { five: { name: 'The Burrito Challenge',
  customers: ['marge', 'gus', 'bev', 'vernon', 'sal', 'oakes', 'rita', 'reginald', 'kai'],
  finale: { customer: 'inferno', items: [{ recipe: 'challengeBurrito', set: { toast: 'extraCrispy' } },
    { recipe: 'chips', set: { salsa: 'greenSalsa' } }] } } }
```

- A crowd gathers to watch Inferno take on the giant burrito, **spoken of, never shown**: the watchers are the drawn
  cast, ordering while they wait (Shift Length orders at level-4 complexity, no visitors, no odd orders).
- The finale, always last: Inferno orders the Challenge Burrito "with every sauce" (said, never made: the ticket is
  hot) and chips with green salsa. "Challenge Burrito: burrito style, white rice, black beans, steak, with cheese,
  lettuce, pico, corn, sour cream, guacamole and jalapeños, hot sauce, extra crispy. Chips and Salsa: green salsa, with
  lime." 17 presses. The giant is drawn 1.6 times bigger, bursts like the Everything Burrito and gets a second giant
  tortilla; it adds no choices. Inferno says his `order.gag` after it (game.js: the finale's customer). If he isn't
  drawn, the first drawn regular (Marge) orders it.
- Mitch: `event.intro`, `event.celebrate`, `event.again` (`{name}`: the event).

