`tests/cast.test.cjs` (who can meet, voices) passes with Hiro listed (his new meetings: Inferno, Rita, Oakes).

## 9. Gross-outs (from level 3)

| id | on | label (`say`) | fx (all the kit's) | What it does |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `brown` | guacamole (an Add, on the line and at the chip basket) | "the brown {name}" → "The brown guacamole." | `tint` #7a6528, `spots` (#4a3a12, 8) | Mitch `gross.brown`; served: `react.gross`, `complain.gross.brown` |
| `hair` | the beans pick: black, pinto | "{name} beans with a hair in them" → "Black beans with a hair in them" | `hair` | as above, `.hair` (pick: `{value}`/`{slot}` lines) |
| `fly` | the chips' salsa pick: red, green, mango | "{name} salsa with a fly in it" → "Red salsa with a fly in it" | `fly` (game.js plays `buzz` for the id `fly`) | as above, `.fly` (pick lines) |

Swap It replaces it and asks again; Skip (on the guacamole) sends it away, a missing-topping mistake if the ticket
wanted it; another value on a pick is a pick mistake. The receipt says e.g. "Beans: black beans with a hair in them".
Burnt is Timed's last stage instead; the bursting burrito is a flourish (spec 4.6).

## 10. For food-burrito: every look, set, flourish and cook

`made()` of a burrito: `{ recipe, ing: 'burrito', parts: [{ ing: 'cheese' }, { ing: 'guacamole', gross? }, ...],
gross, picks: { style, rice, beans, protein, sauce, toast }, counts: {}, auto: ['wrap'] }` (`auto` grows as the
flourishes run: `wrap`, then `burst` on the Everything and Challenge burritos). **There is no `made.done`: the toast is
a `want`, so read it from `made.picks.toast`** (and `o.stage` on the griddle). Tacos: `ing: 'tacos'`, picks `{ style,
protein, sauce, toast }`, `auto: ['fold']`. A bowl: `ing: 'bowl'`, picks `{ style, rice, beans, protein, sauce }`, `auto:
['arrange']`, never toasted. Chips: `{ recipe: 'chips', ing: 'chips', parts: [guacamole?, lime?], picks: { salsa } }`.
**No station `builds`**: `k.sequence` gives the item's **body** (`burrito`, `bowl`, `tacos`, `chips`; its `done` is
undefined) and then the parts in line order: the style value, the rice value, the beans value, the protein value, the
toppings, the sauce value. **Recipe looks name the layout** (`layoutOf` reads `pack.recipes[made.recipe].look.shape`):
`burrito`, `bowl`, `tacos`, `chipsBasket`, `giantBurrito`. The vessel the player sees is the **style picked**
(`made.picks.style`), so a bowl picked for a burrito ticket is drawn as a bowl.

| look.shape | used by | set(s) | how it looks | with cooking (`made.picks.toast`, or `o.stage` on the griddle) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `burritoBody` | ingredient `burrito` (the body) | all | draws nothing of its own (the tortilla is the style value); `look.ramp` is the tortilla's colour at each toast stage (the griddle plates' swatches) | the ramp |
| `tacoBody` | ingredient `tacos` | all | as `burritoBody`, the taco tortillas' ramp | the ramp |
| `bowlBody` | ingredient `bowl` | all | draws nothing (the bowl is the style value) | none |
| `chipBasket` | ingredient `chips` (the side's body) | prep (chip basket), counter | a red-and-white checked paper boat heaped with triangular tortilla chips (`k.heap`), salt specks | none |
| `flourTortilla` | style `burrito` | prep, griddle, counter | a big round flour tortilla, toasty freckles, laid flat on a square of foil; the fillings go in a band down its middle | its colour from the ramp |
| `burritoBowl` | style `bowl` | prep, counter | a wide, shallow bowl, orange (#e8792b) with a green rim stripe (the theme) | none |
| `softTacos` | style `tacos` | prep, griddle, counter | three small soft tortillas, open, side by side in a steel zigzag taco holder | the ramp |
| `rice` | rice `whiteRice` #fbf8f0 (cilantro flecks), `brownRice` #c69a5e | prep, counter | a mound of grains (a band in a burrito, a section in a bowl) | none |
| `beans` | beans `black` #2b2230 (glossy), `pinto` #b0703f (speckled) | prep, counter | a band of small oval beans | none |
| `chickenPieces` | protein `chicken` #e0b070 | prep, counter | grilled cubes with dark grill lines | none |
| `steakPieces` | protein `steak` #7a3b22 | prep, counter | seared cubes, a pink centre on cut faces | none |
| `grilledVeggies` | protein `veggies` #4f9a3a | prep, counter | strips of green and red pepper and zucchini half-moons (no onions: Oakes) | none |
| `shreddedCheese` | cheese #f5b83a | prep, counter | orange-yellow shreds | melts a little (glossier) once toasted |
| `shreddedLettuce` | lettuce #8ccf4d | prep, counter | pale green ribbons | none |
| `pico` | pico #d8402c | prep, counter | diced tomato with white onion bits and cilantro flecks | none |
| `cornKernels` | corn #f6d03a | prep, counter | yellow kernels (one `k.scatter`) | none |
| `sourCream` | sour cream #fbf8ef | prep, counter | a white dollop with a swirl peak; **white on a cream tortilla needs a cue**: a soft cool shadow under it and a gloss highlight | none |
| `guacamole` | guacamole #7fb93c | prep, chip basket, counter | a lumpy green scoop with darker flecks (on the chips: in a small cup beside them) | none |
| `jalapenoRings` | jalapeños #4f9a2a | prep, counter | **six** separate green rings with pale seeds: Coach Bev counts them, so they must be countable | none |
| `dicedOnions` | onions #f4efe2 (tacos only) | prep, counter | small translucent white cubes; white on cream: a faint lilac edge and shadow | none |
| `hotSauce` | sauce `mildSauce` #8cb83a (1 chili), `mediumSauce` #f08a1c (2), `hotSauce` #d23a16 (3) (`look.chilies`) | prep, counter | waiting: the bottle with that many chili marks on its label (the prep shelf's bottles, no text); on the food a zigzag drizzle of its colour (`k.bead`, path `drizzle`); None draws nothing | none |
| `salsaCup` | salsa `redSalsa` #c8321f, `greenSalsa` #5f9a2e, `mangoSalsa` #f2a531 | chip basket, counter | a small round cup of chunky salsa beside the chips | none |
| `limeWedge` | lime #8fd14f | chip basket, counter | a lime wedge on the basket's rim | none |
| `burrito` | recipe look: every burrito but the giant | layout | **before `wrap`**: the flat tortilla on its foil, the fillings in a band down the middle in line order, the sauce zigzag on top. **After `wrap`** (in `made.auto`): a fat rolled burrito, ends tucked, its bottom half in foil, the top end open showing a cross-section of the fillings' colours. **After `burst`**: the same in a second tortilla (two tortilla edges at the open end, the inner one peeking out), a few beans and a smear on the foil | the tortilla by `made.picks.toast` (`o.stage` on the griddle): colour plus press stripes (below) |
| `bowl` | recipe look: both bowls | layout | **before `arrange`**: rice and beans in the bottom, the protein and toppings in loose heaps; **after `arrange`**: every part its own tidy wedge or row, nothing touching (Vernon's whole personality), the sauce zigzag across | none |
| `tacos` | recipe look: both tacos | layout | the holder with three tortillas; **before `fold`**: open, each with the protein and toppings in it (small); **after `fold`**: each folded into a half-moon, fillings showing at the top edge; on the griddle (the cook view) the three lie in a row out of the holder | colour plus press stripes |
| `chipsBasket` | recipe look of `chips` | layout | the checked paper boat of chips, the salsa cup beside it, the guacamole cup if added, the lime wedge on the rim | none |
| `giantBurrito` | recipe look of `challengeBurrito`, `giant: true` | layout | the `burrito` layout, drawn giant by the kit (1.6×; cap it on prep and the griddle with `giantMax`), a little red pennant with a flame (no text) stuck in its top; it bursts and gets a second giant tortilla like the Everything Burrito | as `burrito` |

**The toast, stage by stage** (the griddle's cook view and the counter): doneness shows as a colour AND a mark, and
neighbouring stages differ at the cook view's size by both. The ramp is the ingredient's `look.ramp`.

| stage | colour (burrito ramp) | mark |
|---|---|---|
| soft | pale cream #f3e3bf | no stripes, matt |
| lightlyToasted | light gold #eccb8a | two faint golden press stripes |
| toasted | golden brown #d9a356 | three brown stripes, toasty spots |
| extraCrispy | deep brown #b5732c | four dark stripes, blistered crisp edges |
| burnt | charcoal #3e2614 | black all over, smoke wisps |

**Sets** (measure your own lines, food.md 4; the pictures were asked for prep 62 and griddle 65: the prep's plain
steel counter starts at y 635 of 1024 by its generation notes, the griddle's dark plate at about y 666-730):

- `counter`: `line 0.80`, `surface { y, back }`, its own camera (copy the pizza's `counter.arrange`, food.md 5). As the
  court picture draws the Burritos counter: a **cream top** (about #f6ead2) with a **bright orange plank front**
  (about #f07a14) and a dark brown trim line, the counter picture's returns orange. The order lies flat on the top
  between the Pause sign and the painted queue: `BBArt.burrito.counter.queue` is x 0.564-0.835 (the sunflower woman,
  the sun hat, the man fanning his mouth), heads from 0.462, feet 0.665; read it from the manifest, never measure
  again (2b-seams). A burrito lies along x, a bowl and tacos are low: everything stays flat; a main and chips side by
  side, two mains side by side, the giant alone shrunk to fit.
- `prep`: the plain steel counter below the steam table. The vessel (the style picked) low and left of centre, the
  next ingredient on the right (`incoming`: a heap in a steel pan or tin, the kit's `tin`), `giantMax` for the giant.
  Its `pick` hook: `style` sets the base down (tortilla on foil, bowl, or taco holder); `rice`, `beans`, `protein` spoon
  a scoop from the pan into the band; `sauce` tips that bottle and zigzags it on (None: nothing); on the chip basket
  `salsa` sets the cup down. Its `auto` (or `autos`): **`burritoWrap`** (the sides fold in, it rolls up from the near
  edge, the foil folds round its bottom half), **`tacoFold`** (each tortilla flops over its filling, one after another),
  **`bowlArrange`** (the parts slide into tidy sections, a small settle), **`burritoBurst`** (the wrapped burrito
  bulges, wobbles and pops along its seam; beans, rice and a dab of sour cream arc out onto the foil with a puff of
  steam; then a second tortilla flops over and rolls round it). Every flourish resolves at once under Reduced. A
  flourish whose style was not picked (a bowl picked for a burrito ticket) plays nothing, or the kit's `pop`, and never
  throws.
- `griddle`: the dark steel griddle (the press hangs open, painted, above). `cook: 'griddle'`: `show(c, s)` draws the
  item at `s.stage` (a wrapped burrito lies across the plate; tacos lie in a row); Simple's `run` toasts it to the
  chosen stage (steam puffs, the stripes appear one by one, a little hiss of steam at the end); Timed: it toasts on a
  stage at a time, smoke at burnt. The Timed control prop is the page's `grillPress`. Nothing is drawn above the food
  (the page draws the tool).

Gross-out fx are the kit's (`tint`, `spots`, `hair`, `fly`); the hair lies across the bean band, the fly sits on the
salsa cup's surface.

## 11. Sounds

`prep`: `auto: 'wrap'` (every flourish, the burst included until the page plays `burst`: Requests); `griddle`: `cook:
'press'` (the press comes down: Simple when the stage is chosen, Timed when the clock starts). Every Add plays the
default `plop`, each Timed stage `tick`. The page plays `swoosh` (Skip), `toss` (Swap It), `buzz` (the gross-out id
`fly`), `ding`, `kaching`, `stars`, `ew` as for the diner. All exist (`packs/burrito/sound`, `packs/shared/sound`);
`tests/voices.test.cjs` checks them. `burst` (`packs/burrito/sound/burst.wav`) waits for the page (audio.md 5.2 lists
it as the page's, "with the bursting-burrito joke").

## 12. For the script: every moment and who must say it

`SC.moments(pack)` on the merged pack: 57 moments, 240 coverage items with an empty script. **Written** (content-burrito, 2026-11-09): `packs/burrito/script.js`, 384 lines, `SC.check` and `SC.coverage` both empty; conventions and counts in `docs/api/packs/burrito-script.md`. F = the pack's 'customer'
fallback lines count for anyone with fewer than two of their own.

- **Customers, everyone** (marge gus bev vernon sal oakes inferno rita reginald kai hiro): `greet` ×3, `smalltalk` ×3,
  `goodbye` ×3 (the cast script supplies these for the regulars and visitors; **inferno, rita and hiro need their own
  here**); `react.3`/`.2`/`.1` ×3 of their own; F: `react.gross`, `complain.extra`/`.unasked`/`.missing` ({ing}{ings}),
  `complain.done` ({want}: stage words), `complain.pick` ({slot}{want}), `complain.more`, `complain.gross.brown`
  ({ing}), `complain.gross.hair` and `.fly` (pick gross-outs: {value}{slot}).
- **Some**: `visitor.arrive` reginald kai hiro; `order.usual` marge; `order.twin` gus; `order.dislike` sal (lettuce),
  oakes (onions); `order.gag` inferno, rita (locals at home, ≤ 8 s; Inferno's also after the event finale);
  `react.favourite` bev (she counts the jalapeños), inferno, rita; F `order.odd.doubleWrap`, `.noAvocado`, `.hottest`,
  `.justTortilla` (the regulars and Rita) and `.fireAlarm` (Inferno).
- **Mitch** (2 each unless 1): `shift.start`, `shift.end`, `uniform` (1); `tutorial.intro`, `.ticket`, `.review`,
  `.serve`, `.gross`; `tutorial.prep`, `.griddle`, `.chips`, `tutorial.cook.griddle`;
  `tutorial.warn.extra`/`.unasked`/`.missing`/`.done`/`.pick`/`.gross`/`.grossSkip`; `gross.brown` ({ing}), `.hair`,
  `.fly` ({value}); `nearly` ({want}{name}), `after.3`, `after.1`, `after.gross`, `event.intro`/`.celebrate`/`.again`
  ({name}) (1).
- **Not needed**: `complain.tooMany`/`.tooFew` and their warnings (no Add with a max above 1, no repeat).
- **Blank words**: {slot} style, rice, beans, protein, hot sauce, salsa; {want}/{got} burrito, bowl, tacos, white,
  brown, none, black, pinto, chicken, steak, veggies, mild, medium, hot, red, green, mango; stages lightly toasted,
  toasted, extra crispy, soft, burnt; {ing} cheese, lettuce, pico, corn, sour cream, guacamole, jalapeños, onions,
  lime, or burrito / tacos for `done`. Pick lines say "for the {slot}, I said {want}" ("for the hot sauce, I said
  none"). Pick gross-out lines say "{value} beans" and "{value} salsa".
- **The brief**: Inferno wants it hotter (smoke from his ears; the four-chili bottle on the shelf is never on a
  ticket); Rita's "one of everything" (said, never made); Marge's bean and cheese usual; Gus's two burritos
  (`order.twin`); Bev counts the jalapeños out loud (her favourite: six of them); Vernon's bowl, nothing touching;
  Sal's steak, never lettuce; Oakes's new onion reason (tacos); Chef Hiro judges the roll; the odd orders as in
  section 6; the tutorial customer is Rita ("she"); the finale is Inferno's.

## 13. Help

The pack's `help` (Pause > Help): "Ben's Burritos. Every order starts at the burrito line: pick the style, Burrito, Bowl
or Tacos, then the rice, the beans and the protein. Then Add or Skip each topping as it comes down the line, and pick the
hot sauce. A burrito wraps itself, and tacos fold themselves. Then the griddle: in Simple, pick how toasted, Lightly
Toasted, Toasted or Extra Crispy; in Timed, the press comes down, so Lift the Press when it reaches the stage on the
ticket. Bowls skip the griddle; tacos skip the rice and beans and get onions. Chips and salsa: pick the salsa, then Add
or Skip the guacamole and the lime. The ticket lists everything: add what's on it, skip what isn't. If something looks
wrong, Swap It brings a fresh one."

