## 15. The tutorial

Rita (the restaurant's own); one guided order through every station: "Chicken Burrito: burrito style, white rice,
black beans, chicken, with cheese, lettuce, pico, sour cream and guacamole, mild sauce, toasted. Chips and Salsa: red
salsa, with lime." The guacamole comes down the line brown (`gross: { item: 0, ing: 'guacamole', event: 'brown' }`), so
Swap It is taught once. Always Simple; Mitch warns before each mistake. 17 presses done right, plus the Swap It: 18.

## 16. Press counts (`pressReport('burrito')`, Serve included; Simple and Timed alike, the same at every level)

| recipe | levels | presses |
|---|---|---|
| chickenBurrito, steakBurrito, beanCheese | 1-5 | 14 (style, rice, beans, protein, 7 toppings, sauce, griddle, Serve) |
| chickenBowl | 1-5 | 13 (no griddle) |
| veggieBowl | 2-5 | 13 |
| steakTacos, chickenTacos | 2-5 | 13 (style, protein, 7 toppings, onions, sauce, griddle, Serve) |
| chips | 2-5 | 4 (salsa, guacamole, lime, Serve) |
| everythingBurrito, fireBurrito | 3-5 | 14 |
| challengeBurrito (event) | event | 14 alone; the finale with chips 17 |

Whole orders (bots, 1500 orders a level in each mode): levels 1 and 2 at most 14; levels 3-5 and the event at most 28
(Gus's two burritos, 27, plus a Swap It); a burrito with chips 17 (18 with a Swap It); every odd order 13 or 14; the
tutorial 18. Budget (spec 4.3): level 1 ≤ 14, any order ≤ 28: both met, the second exactly.

## 17. Requests (for the owners named)

- **page / whoever owns `index.html`**: done by this lane under the shared-file rules (`packs/burrito/pack.js` after the
  cafe's lines; `packs/burrito/script.js` once it exists); the food line is food-burrito's to ask for.
- **page**: play `burrito`'s `burst` for an auto event whose id is `burst` (audio.md 5.2 lists it as the page's); until
  then the station's `wrap` plays for it (game.js plays the station's one `sounds.auto` for every flourish). The
  griddle's Timed control is already drawn as the `grillPress` prop (stage.js `tool`, from the shared props manifest),
  labelled "Lift the Press".
- **food-burrito**: section 10: 23 shapes, 5 layouts, sets `counter`, `prep` (also the chip basket) and `griddle` (cook
  `griddle`), four flourishes (`burritoWrap`, `tacoFold`, `bowlArrange`, `burritoBurst`), the toast stages by colour and
  stripes, the toast read from `made.picks.toast`.
